Proposed (25.7s): Go tests, at every stage: write or generate a package's `_test.go`; review or critique tests someone else wrote; rework a suite that tests one exported symbol at a time or pokes at internals; turn thin assertions into runnable Examples for pkgsite; build a conformance / `httptest`-style testing package so outside implementers can prove they conform; shape an API up front so its tests stay writable. Reach for it too when finishing any Go code, since committed code without contract tests is unfinished. Applies the maintainer's standard: tests state the package's contract with its users, drafted from the exported docs before the source, plain-English property names, one package-level suite over per-symbol tests, a mandatory representative example, typed errors over string matching, and a hard-to-write test read as a redesign signal. Not for non-Go suites, `go vet` or fuzz triage, test-plan documents, or explaining stdlib testing APIs.

